+## 2026-11-03
+- **Matching suggestions treat USD and USDT alike in both directions** ([#65](https://github.com/trysarathy/investigation-desk/pull/65)). When a payment is missing a record, Clearline suggests likely candidates and says why ("same amount", "same asset"). A provider row quoted in USD did not get the "same asset" hint against a USDT instruction, although the reverse did. The hint now works both ways round. USDC and USDT are still never treated as the same asset. Suggestions are only hints; nothing is linked without a person.
+
 ## 2026-11-01
 - **CHANGELOG started.** From today every merged pull request adds an entry here.
